{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QhUGQHs7JGqnvG22Miptt7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://www.ecnlpir.org/reviewerguidelines.html\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 and the review process, though the specific \"Findings reviewer guidelines review form\" document was not directly available in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Structure\n\nSubmissions are performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ACL Rolling Review (ARR), where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, and then authors commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\n## Review Timeline\n\nIf reviewers receive assignments, reviews must be completed by July 6, or meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nFor the specific EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines and review form, you may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website at https://2026.emnlp.org/ or the ACL Rolling Review platform at aclrollingreview.org, as these appear to host the most up-to-date reviewer documentation and forms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e0fab31-3c97-44af-b8df-c308847e2709","uuid":"2d1dbf46-8706-4b0f-8f0d-2135e30cc682","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:20:35.588Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Mb7TU8gWXHHyW5yH3vRh8q","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://www.ecnlpir.org/reviewerguidelines.html"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...","url":"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 and the review process, though the specific \"Findings reviewer guidelines review form\" document was not directly available in the search results. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review Structure\n\nSubmissions are performed via the Open Review platform, where authors submit articles to ACL Rolling Review (ARR), where submissions receive reviews and meta-reviews from ARR reviewers and action editors, and then authors commit their reviewed articles to EMNLP 2026, where Senior Area Chairs and Program Chairs make acceptance decisions from the ARR reviews and meta-reviews.\n\n## Review Timeline\n\nIf reviewers receive assignments, reviews must be completed by July 6, or meta-reviews by July 29.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nFor the specific EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines and review form, you may want to check the official EMNLP 2026 website at https://2026.emnlp.org/ or the ACL Rolling Review platform at aclrollingreview.org, as these appear to host the most up-to-date reviewer documentation and forms."],"durationSeconds":4.961002418}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012DPDRkvAiy75MSCS3j5fuG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and review form:\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections. The first section is an In-Depth Review for your overall assessment of the paper, which includes 3 subsections, with the core review being the most important part.\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nA 5 point scale with half point increments is used. A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, though reviewers should try to take a stand by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, unless they truly consider it a borderline paper.\n\n## Key Review Criteria\n\n**Core Review:** This should include your view of the main contributions that the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds, significant strong and weak parts, and how the work advances the state of knowledge in computational linguistics.\n\n**Reproducibility:** Reviewers must answer \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5. There's also a question about whether the authors' Reproducibility Checklist answers are useful, with three options provided: very useful, somewhat useful, or not useful.\n\n**Reasons to Accept:** Reviewers should briefly summarize the main reasons why the paper should be accepted and how the NLP community would benefit from it.\n\nThe official EMNLP 2025 reviewer instructions are available at https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e0fab31-3c97-44af-b8df-c308847e2709","uuid":"3393ce11-f667-4204-8854-380e55c4d90f","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:20:36.769Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_019qQ2NWPrgdKEFFs6a8GGfy","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about the EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and review form:\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections. The first section is an In-Depth Review for your overall assessment of the paper, which includes 3 subsections, with the core review being the most important part.\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nA 5 point scale with half point increments is used. A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, though reviewers should try to take a stand by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, unless they truly consider it a borderline paper.\n\n## Key Review Criteria\n\n**Core Review:** This should include your view of the main contributions that the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds, significant strong and weak parts, and how the work advances the state of knowledge in computational linguistics.\n\n**Reproducibility:** Reviewers must answer \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5. There's also a question about whether the authors' Reproducibility Checklist answers are useful, with three options provided: very useful, somewhat useful, or not useful.\n\n**Reasons to Accept:** Reviewers should briefly summarize the main reasons why the paper should be accepted and how the NLP community would benefit from it.\n\nThe official EMNLP 2025 reviewer instructions are available at https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"],"durationSeconds":5.470997481999999}}
