{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TPi3gTKg4J8B5UdihtirGo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall assessment scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"}]\n\nI found the information from the ACL Rolling Review's review form. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n**Soundness Scale:**\nThe soundness assessment uses a scale where 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies of its type), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n**Excitement Scale:**\nFor excitement, 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend the paper to others and/or attend its presentation) and 4 = Exciting (would mention the paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation).\n\n**Overall Assessment Scale:**\nThe overall assessment uses a scale including: 5 = Consider for Award (top 2.5% papers), 2 = Resubmit next cycle (needs substantial revisions by next cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (needs substantial revisions that cannot be completed by next cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit (requires full redo or isn't relevant to the *ACL community).\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e0fab31-3c97-44af-b8df-c308847e2709","uuid":"1176b9ad-2798-4d64-9c51-516ef725de9c","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:20:53.257Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"site:aclrollingreview.org reviewform soundness excitement overall assessment scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01FiFeSUQvJTY74HJS1HKC7a","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"}]},"I found the information from the ACL Rolling Review's review form. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n**Soundness Scale:**\nThe soundness assessment uses a scale where 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies of its type), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims).\n\n**Excitement Scale:**\nFor excitement, 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend the paper to others and/or attend its presentation) and 4 = Exciting (would mention the paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation).\n\n**Overall Assessment Scale:**\nThe overall assessment uses a scale including: 5 = Consider for Award (top 2.5% papers), 2 = Resubmit next cycle (needs substantial revisions by next cycle), 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle (needs substantial revisions that cannot be completed by next cycle), and 1 = Do not resubmit (requires full redo or isn't relevant to the *ACL community)."],"durationSeconds":3.7151310710000036}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QBkArvgxZUv2WpAirrfLoj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form \"overall assessment\" \"5\" \"4\" \"3\" \"2\" \"1\" scale description\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 February | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FFebruary\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 July | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FJuly\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 October | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FOctober\"}]\n\nI found information about the ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form. Let me search for more specific details about the complete scale descriptions.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Proposal - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Rolling_Review_Proposal\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"Allen Cognitive Level - StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK556125/\"}]\n\nBased on my search results, I found the ACL Rolling Review 2025 overall assessment scale descriptions. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n## Overall Assessment Scale (5-1 Scale)\n\n**5 = Excellent:** This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n\n**4 = Strong:** This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n\n**3 = Acceptable:** This study provides sufficient support for its main claims. Some minor points may need extra support or details.\n\n**2 = Poor:** Some of the main claims are not sufficiently supported. There are major technical/methodological problems.\n\n**1 = Major Issues:** This study is not yet sufficiently thorough to warrant publication or is not relevant to ACL.\n\nAdditionally, the Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2e0fab31-3c97-44af-b8df-c308847e2709","uuid":"601ff8ea-a6e4-4332-8010-1845d75faa43","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:20:58.409Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2025 review form \"overall assessment\" \"5\" \"4\" \"3\" \"2\" \"1\" scale description","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BYtmdUXWsEVwQsS3DVBTYC","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines –